#
# Forces LF on every text file regardless of platform, so a Windows checkout
# doesn't show every line of every file as changed against LF-committed
# history. LF specifically (not just platform-native) because *.sh scripts
# run inside a Linux devcontainer/target host — a CRLF shebang fails to
# exec — and Ansible's embedded shell blocks would carry a stray \r into
# whatever runs on the remote host too.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Leave certs byte-exact rather than trusting text auto-detection.
*.pem -text
